@node Top
@top beads.el

@insertcopying

This is the manual for @code{beads.el}, a Magit-like Emacs interface
for the @uref{https://github.com/steveyegge/beads, Beads} issue
tracker.  It is built by the project's autotools front door and
installed as GNU Info.

@menu
* Introduction::                What beads.el is and what it needs.
* Building and installing::     The autotools build and install targets.
@end menu

@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@code{beads.el} exposes the @command{bd} command-line issue tracker from
inside Emacs through transient menus, tabulated issue lists, and a
VUI-based dashboard.  Every user-visible command is derived from the
@command{bd} subcommand inventory.

@node Building and installing
@chapter Building and installing

The project builds with the standard GNU toolchain:

@example
./autogen.sh && ./configure && make && make install
@end example

@noindent
@code{make} byte-compiles the package with warnings treated as errors and
generates @file{beads-autoloads.el}.  @code{make install} installs the
Elisp files and the Info manual.  @xref{Top,,, dir, Directory of
installed manuals}, for how to browse it.

@bye
